 "head": {
  "text": "WF-029 Bit time segments, sample point and transmit point (1 clock = 1 time quantum)"
 },
 "foot": {
  "text": "Bit time of 10 time quanta: SYNC_SEG 1, PROP_SEG + PHASE_SEG1 6, PHASE_SEG2 3, SJW 2. The pin edge of SOF at clock 20 reaches rx_s two clocks later (two-flop synchronizer) and hard-synchronizes the counter: that clock is SYNC_SEG. The sample point is the end of the last SEG1 quantum; the transmit point is the start of SYNC_SEG of the next bit."
 }
